@moduledoc """
The application's UI kit, on top of Phoenix's CoreComponents and daisyUI.

`use <%= inspect(@web) %>.UI` (already in `<%= inspect(@web) %>.html_helpers/0`) imports:

  * `<%= inspect(@web) %>.UI.Components`: page headers, cards, stat grids, badges, alerts,
    description lists, tabs, modals, dropdowns, avatars, feeds, empty states,
    form sections, pagination and search inputs,
  * `<%= inspect(@web) %>.UI.Shell`: the app shell (sidebar or top navigation), nav items and
    the user menu,
  * `<%= inspect(@web) %>.UI.DataTable`: a searchable, sortable, paginated table,

and aliases `<%= inspect(@web) %>.UI.ListState`, the in-memory search/sort/paging state the
table renders.

Every component styles itself with daisyUI's semantic colors (`base-*`,
`primary`, …) and radii, so the themepack in `assets/css/app.css` restyles all
of them, in light and dark. The pack and the shell it uses are configured in
`config/config.exs`:

    config :<%= @app %>, <%= inspect(@web) %>.UI, themepack: "<%= @themepack.name %>", shell: :<%= @themepack.shell %>

Switch packs with `mix tinderbox.gen.ui --themepack <ember|slate|harbor>`. See
every component, live, at `/dev/ui` (dev only).
"""

defmacro __using__(_opts) do
  quote do
    import <%= inspect(@web) %>.UI.Components
    import <%= inspect(@web) %>.UI.Shell
    import <%= inspect(@web) %>.UI.DataTable
    alias <%= inspect(@web) %>.UI.ListState
  end
end
